  "final_message": "{\"summary\":\"Implemented and verified `safeUploadPath`. It now accepts one filename component, resolves it lexically under `baseDir`, and rejects empty/non-string input, NUL bytes, `.`/`..`, both separators, absolute paths, and drive-qualified names. Study Note: this function validates untrusted upload filenames before downstream storage; it constructs a path only and performs no filesystem access. Before, it always threw TODO; now valid names resolve beneath the base directory while unsafe names throw. The compact guard centralizes component validation before `path.resolve`. Truth status: verified.\",\"files_changed\":[\"src/upload-path.mjs\"],\"tests_run\":[\"`node --test` — passed: 1 test, 0 failures\",\"Focused security assertions — passed for traversal, separators, absolute/drive-qualified names, empty input, NUL, and non-string values\"],\"remaining_uncertainty\":[\"Symlink-safe creation remains intentionally outside this function; downstream writes must use no-follow or equivalent exclusive-open semantics.\",\"No meaningful implementation tasks remain.\"]}",
